## Mandatory rules

- `GATE-01` and `GATE-02`: use the task classes, authorization gates, protected
  boundaries, and scope-change procedure defined only in
  `docs/CODEX_WORKFLOW.md`; do not invent a local exception.
- `WORKTREE-01`: preserve existing work; do not reset, clean, overwrite,
  commit, rewrite history, or reformat unrelated files.
- `EVIDENCE-01`: use only verified project facts and commands. Record unknowns
  as documentation gaps; do not invent policy or install discovery tools.
- `CONTEXT-01`: use `.agents/ai/project-map.json` and
  `docs/AI_CONTEXT_STRATEGY.md`; start bounded and expand only for a named
  evidence trigger.
- `MODULE-01`: preserve documented module responsibilities, dependency
  direction, contracts, and shared-library gates.
- `VERIFY-01`: select evidenced scope-relevant checks through
  `docs/VERIFICATION.md`; command selection never authorizes execution, and
  not-run never means pass.
- `ADAPT-01`: apply the evidence, confirmation, and protected-boundary rules in
  `docs/CODEX_WORKFLOW.md` and `docs/CODING_RULES_LOG.md`.
- For every new or materially changed source file, detect its language and apply
  the selected industry profile in `docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md`. Treat verified
  build, compatibility, security, privacy, and public-contract requirements as
  hard constraints; record rather than hide conflicts with existing conventions.
- Keep the verified architecture and dependency direction:

  {{ARCHITECTURE_SUMMARY}}
- Add or update tests in proportion to changed behavior.
- Record concise L1/L2 impact in `docs/TASK_TEMPLATE.md`; use
  `docs/CHANGE_IMPACT.md` for the full L3/L4 trace.
- Finish with `git diff --check`, relevant diff/status review, and a report of unverified items and residual risk.

## Workflow entrypoints

- New feature or fix: follow `docs/CODEX_WORKFLOW.md`; use
  `docs/TASK_TEMPLATE.md` when a durable task record is useful.
- Large or unfamiliar task: use `$context-discovery` before proposing scope.
- Build and test: use `$build-and-test` or follow `docs/VERIFICATION.md`.
- Review: use `$code-review`; a review-only request does not authorize fixes.
- Coding rules: follow `docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md`, its selected language
  profiles, enforcement sources, and `docs/CODING_RULES_LOG.md`.
- Architecture, ADR, module-map, shared-library, performance, and skill-design
  guidance is optional and applies only when listed in the generated template
  state and selected from verified project evidence.
